 intro:
 'A dog or cat leaves mainland China for Dubai from Beijing Capital (PEK), Shanghai Pudong (PVG) or Guangzhou Baiyun (CAN). Hong Kong International (HKG) appears only as a via-Hong-Kong routing note. It is not a mainland origin and not an AFCD export. UAE arrival is a MOCCAE import permit valid for 90 days from issuance, with cargo release at Dubai International (DXB) or Al Maktoum / Dubai World Central (DWC). Air China, China Eastern, Emirates and Cathay Pacific are cargo. There is no cabin flag and no Qatar Airways row on this route.',
 snippetQuestion: 'How do I fly a pet from Shanghai or Beijing to Dubai?',
 snippetAnswer:
 'Confirm live-animal export at Shanghai Pudong (PVG), Beijing Capital (PEK) or Guangzhou Baiyun (CAN), and keep that code on the certificate and the booking. Hold a MOCCAE import permit that is still inside its 90 days from issuance. Plan cargo release at Dubai International (DXB) or Al Maktoum / Dubai World Central (DWC). Air China, China Eastern, Emirates and Cathay Pacific are cargo. HKG on this route is a via note, not the origin airport.',
